After reviewing design files for this solution I find the layout and buttons of the windows forms are thought out and easy to read. 
I do like the simple layout of the forms. Unfortunately while this program does work, it does not have the sorting and filtering options 
present for further review. In the .cs files I see good method layouts, just not the use of sql queries or linq or the methods for 
sorting/filtering. What I would change is further setting up the forms with back color, group boxes, radio buttons, etc. then calling 
sql queries built in the database .xsd designer to keep it simple. I would also include comments to explain the methods as well as a 
comment for name, assignment, class, etc. to help clarify whose project it is. I also found that Linq worked well for my version of 
the project if you want to take a look. 
